     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin-bottom:10px;color:rgb(85,85,85);font-family:&#39;Source Sans Pro&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif\">I attempted building shiny-server from source using the guidelines for &quot;other platforms&quot; provided by RStudio.</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin-bottom:10px;color:rgb(85,85,85);font-family:&#39;Source Sans Pro&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif\">I have modified the launcher.cc file for a Mac as suggested elsewhere</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin-bottom:10px;color:rgb(85,85,85);font-family:&#39;Source Sans Pro&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif\">At the &quot;sudo make install&quot; step in RStudio guide I get the following error message:<br></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin-bottom:10px;color:rgb(85,85,85);font-family:&#39;Source Sans Pro&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif\">CMake Error at cmake_install.cmake:31 (file):</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin-bottom:10px;color:rgb(85,85,85);font-family:&#39;Source Sans Pro&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif\">  file INSTALL cannot find</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin-bottom:10px;color:rgb(85,85,85);font-family:&#39;Source Sans Pro&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif\">  &quot;/my/download/directory/shiny-server/node_modules&quot;.</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin-bottom:10px;color:rgb(85,85,85);font-family:&#39;Source Sans Pro&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif\">I have verified that the download from GitHub does not include node-modules.</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin-bottom:10px;color:rgb(85,85,85);font-family:&#39;Source Sans Pro&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif\">All the other build and installation steps seem to work just fine. Are the current guidelines at RStudio out of date? What am I missing?</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin-bottom:10px;color:rgb(85,85,85);font-family:&#39;Source Sans Pro&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif\">Thanks for any help</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;margin-bottom:10px;color:rgb(85,85,85);font-family:&#39;Source Sans Pro&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif\">Tom aka Dr. Wo</p></div>"
